Maybe the solution is to modify ggplot_build() and explicitly have it set default expand values early in the pipeline. This would require interaction of coords and scales earlier in the process  than presently happens.

This is different from how my modifications work now: the default expand values are set when coord_train() is called, and this is the last thing in ggplot_build().

Setting default expand values early would actually simplify some of the code, though I don't know if it might be problematic in other ways.

-Winston

